WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.958
A heart says it. A reply answers one message. This is react and reply.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.281
Press and hold a message, or focus it and press Enter. Message actions opens.

00:00:13.481 --> 00:00:17.200
Five quick reactions, More reactions, Reply and Copy.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.400
Pick the heart. A chip shows under the message: the heart, its count, and pressed,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.720
because it's yours.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.920
Choose your chip again, and your reaction goes. A chip that reaches zero goes too.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.188
More reactions has twelve more, pancakes among them.

00:00:37.388 --> 00:00:39.923
And what the others choose shows as it happens.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.029
If a reaction doesn't save, it goes back, and says so, with Try again.

00:00:48.229 --> 00:00:50.515
Copy puts the message on the clipboard.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.841
Reply shows Replying to Ruth, one line of her message, and Cancel reply.

00:00:59.041 --> 00:01:03.112
Send, and your reply carries a quote: her first name and one line.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.565
Choose a quote, and the thread goes to that message and marks it for two seconds,

00:01:10.565 --> 00:01:12.894
loading earlier messages if it must.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.430
On your own message, there is Delete too. It asks first: Delete this message?

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:24.282
A reply to it stays, and its quote reads Message deleted.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.582
In a direct message, it all works the same way, and only the two of you see it.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.284
On a phone, Message actions rises from the bottom.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.606
From a tablet up, it opens over the thread.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.552
Once the Popkin wraps up, chips and quotes stay, but nothing can be changed.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.224
What no screen shows: one reaction per member per emoji, held by the API, and a

00:02:03.224 --> 00:02:07.955
version on each message's reactions, so an older update never wins.

00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:13.068
A direct message's reactions reach its two members alone, and no log carries the

00:02:13.068 --> 00:02:13.736
emoji.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.616
That is journey twelve. Popkin is a free platform for pop-up communities.
